cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "gunfolds: Causal Structure Learning from Undersampled Time Series"
version: 0.0.7
date-released: 2023-01-01
license: MIT
url: "https://neuroneural.github.io/gunfolds/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/neuroneural/gunfolds"
authors:
  - family-names: Abavisani
    given-names: Sajad
    email: s.abavisani@gatech.edu
    affiliation: "Georgia Institute of Technology"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-7702-2340"
abstract: >
  gunfolds is a Python toolkit for causal structure learning from undersampled
  time series, with a focus on scalable constraint-based methods using Answer
  Set Programming (ASP). It includes implementations of GRACE-C (rate-agnostic
  causal estimation via constraints, achieving 1000x speedup over prior
  methods), RnR (a meta-solver that refines any causal discovery algorithm for
  undersampled data), dRASL, and ION-C.
keywords:
  - causal discovery
  - time series
  - undersampling
  - answer set programming
  - fMRI
  - graphical models
